<title>UK: Libya leaves crude prices unchanged for January.</title>
<headline>Libya leaves crude prices unchanged for January.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libya kept oil export price formulas unchanged for January loadings, traders said.</p>
<p>Libya told customers Es Sider would sell at Dated Brent +10 cents for January, unchanged from December.</p>
<p>Zueitina and Brega were priced at Dated Brent +40 cents.</p>
<p>Sarir was left at Dated Brent -55 cents, Bu Attifel at Brent -30 cents, Amna at Brent -60 cents and Sirtica at Brent +15 cents.</p>
<p>Bouri was priced at Iranian Heavy fob Sidi Kreir -35 cents.</p>
<p>-- Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
